`sheriff approve --withdraw <sid>...` withdraws the approval of each wording of the node for which one stands, whether the node holds that wording or not. For each such wording it appends a line: the node's sid, that wording's fingerprint, `withdrawn: true` and, as `by`, the email git is configured with. It makes the node a draft. Where no approval stands for any wording of the node, it appends nothing. Anyone may run it. It refuses:

